    "completed_datetime": "08/28/2024 10:30 AM",
    "comments": "Preston Ellexson - 08/28/24  8:31:15 AM: Used our hydraulic power press kit. Put a 1 1/2\" piece of square tubing into the building beam for support. Got the beam pushed back out to where it should be. Took a few tries due to lack of space and adapters. Tested bay door. It got really hard about 3' from the floor and stayed hard to shut. Opened the width of the c purlin back up since it was hit so hard. After that and adjusted with a mallet, the door is opening very easily. It locks smoothly and door is working good. I couldn't straighten everything out, but since the door is smooth and functional, I'm leaving it alone.",
    "attachments": []
  },
  {
