    "work_performed_by": "Preston",
    "assigned_to": "Maintenance",
    "downtime_hours": "0",
    "completed_datetime": "06/16/2022 02:30 PM",
    "comments": "Preston Ellexson - 07/21/22  7:30:07 AM: Removed all wires and components from the existing system. Bought 2 new 120V pumps. Ran new fittings up and out of the pit. Cleaned a lot of the trash out. Made expanded metal risers for each pump. Changed some of the wiring that goes to the shipping docks and lights, etc. Labeled entire electrical panel and changed some breakers around to get these pumps tied in. Put a single gang electrical outlet in the pvc box right inside. Pumps have floats built in. | Preston Ellexson - 06/02/22 12:38:01 PM: The pumps weren't working this morning so the docks were full of water. The first contactor looks really burned up again. One of the pumps is pulling about 3X the current draw in comparison to the other. Went and bought a new pump, fittings, and water hose. Got it hooked up to run until it's empty. I turned off power to the pumps for now. Tomorrow I will clean the electrical components and go from there.",
    "attachments": []
  },
  {
    "equipment_id": "1392",
    "equipment_eq_id": "EQ ID 1392",
    "equipment_name": "Dock Pump",
    "department": "Shipping",
    "wo_id": "2214",
    "date_notified": "08/22/2022",
    "urgency": "3. Prod Affected, Not Stopped",
    "problem": "The pipe to the drain pump is disconnected and not draining properly.",
    "status": "Closed and Completed",
    "material_cost": "0",
    "labor_time": "0.75",
    "work_performed_by": "Mark Zeober",
    "assigned_to": "Maintenance",
    "downtime_hours": "0",
    "completed_datetime": "08/25/2022 10:30 AM",
    "comments": "Mark Zeober - 08/25/22  5:32:17 AM: A different connection came apart on 8/24/22, so I put the pipe back together and disconnected one pump and finished pumping water.  we will continue to monitor. | Mark Zeober - 08/22/22  9:20:43 AM: Nothing is glued together, so it blew apart.  So, I reassembled and glued Just one of the joints, as it was the weakest joint in the system.  the rubber boots were also loose so I tightened them up as well.  If it continues to come apart we may need to shut off one pump.  also wile testing the pump I observed that  the pump floats need to be adjusted to cut off sooner to keep the pumps from sucking air.",
    "attachments": []
  },
