    "assigned_to": "Maintenance",
    "downtime_hours": "0",
    "completed_datetime": "06/03/2022 07:30 AM",
    "comments": "Preston Ellexson - 06/03/22  6:02:19 AM: Power for dock 2 is also tied into the power for one of the sump pumps. Removed wires in sump pump box and put on wire nuts. Turned the power back on for the dock. Tested and everything is working good. Re-fit the clamp for the conduit to the box.",
    "attachments": []
  },
  {
    "equipment_id": "1806",
    "equipment_eq_id": "EQ ID 1806",
    "equipment_name": "Bay #2",
    "department": "Shipping",
    "wo_id": "10742",
    "date_notified": "03/18/2024",
    "urgency": "6. General Maint",
    "problem": "Dock 2 seems low on hydraulic fluid - not raising correctly, button doesnt activate immediately",
    "status": "Closed and Completed",
    "material_cost": "45",
    "labor_time": "1",
    "work_performed_by": "Preston/Charles/Sammy",
    "assigned_to": "Supervisor",
    "downtime_hours": "0",
    "completed_datetime": "03/27/2024 11:30 AM",
    "comments": "Preston Ellexson - 03/27/24 10:34:36 AM: Got the hose removed and replaced with new. Replaced the 3/8\" swivel fitting as well. Topped off the reservoir with light weight hydraulic oil. Tested multiple times with no issues. No leaking on the fittings. I will monitor for a few days. | Preston Ellexson - 03/26/24  6:19:35 AM: Truck is still there. Had Charles hold the ramp open while I put the maintenance safety bar in place. There is a hydraulic hose that is leaking slightly. Got with Dean and I'm letting him figure out a day to do this. I just need to remove the line, go get one made at Jimmie's, and replace it. I'll check the hydraulic level at that time. | Joshua Patton - 03/18/24  9:39:40 AM: spoke with Charles there is a truck in Dock two that supposed to leave Friday when the truck leaves he is going to block off that dock so we can look at it",
    "attachments": []
  },
  {
    "equipment_id": "1806",
    "equipment_eq_id": "EQ ID 1806",
    "equipment_name": "Bay #2",
    "department": "Shipping",
    "wo_id": "11767",
    "date_notified": "05/21/2024",
    "urgency": "5. Prod Ongoing, Maint Required",
    "problem": "The dock plate slow to lift and lower.",
    "status": "Pending",
    "material_cost": "240",
    "labor_time": "2",
    "work_performed_by": "Preston",
    "assigned_to": "Maintenance",
    "downtime_hours": "0",
    "completed_datetime": "03/10/2025 07:00 AM",
    "comments": "Preston Ellexson - 03/10/25  4:42:04 AM: Vendor got with manufacturer. They discontinued this item. In January they were in process of a new run of components to replace this model. Radwell kept us in the loop. Finally received the new starter control. It has a stop on it, so I need to look further to see if that will be possible to install without the stop button working. They just need the start button to engage the pump up and down. | Preston Ellexson - 09/19/24  4:17:19 AM: Reached out to vendor for order update. | Preston Ellexson - 08/27/24  4:12:26 AM: Still awaiting new starter control. | Preston Ellexson - 07/24/24  6:41:32 AM: Lead time was 3-4 weeks. | Preston Ellexson - 07/16/24  4:28:12 AM: Ordered starter on Friday. I will swap out after it arrives around the shipping dept schedule. I'll get with Karen and Chuck on this. | Preston Ellexson - 07/08/24  8:34:01 AM: Awaiting quote for new starter control. | Preston Ellexson - 05/31/24  9:51:19 AM: Dean let me know an operator was asking about the green button to engage the hydraulics. I inspected and found the contact points were all burned up. The auxiliary contact isn't in the best shape. Nothing had actually corroded too bad. Removed contactor, brought to maintenance, and took apart to clean all points. Got all put back together and voltage turned back on. Tested and it is working much better than before. The button is hard to push, but that's just the old style of these controls. Got with Radwell for contactor and aux contact. They are out of stock and discontinued. Looking elsewhere. Dean doesn't want to upgrade the entire control box yet, but I'm going to look for some to get prices. I might have to cross reference and get a different brand contactor that's available. | Preston Ellexson - 05/24/24  8:12:46 AM: Inspected dock. There are no leaks that would cause this. There is plenty of fluid in the reservoir. Motor and pump are running. No strange noises during operation. Dock just goes pretty slow when raising. I'm going to get with Dean on Monday for a service visit from Johnson Equipment Company. | Preston Ellexson - 05/21/24 12:23:19 PM: Got with Karen and Dean on this. I'm going to inspect it tomorrow between swapping out forklift PM's. If there are no leaks and nothing visibly wrong, I'll get in touch with Johnson Equipment Company to come out and inspect. Might be a pump going bad.",
    "attachments": []
  },
  {
    "equipment_id": "1807",
    "equipment_eq_id": "EQ ID 1807",
    "equipment_name": "Bay #3",
    "department": "Shipping",
    "wo_id": "17914",
    "date_notified": "12/11/2025",
    "urgency": "6. General Maint",
    "problem": "Hello Maintenance team,\n\nPlease add to your schedule some time to grease the dock plates and perform any additional maintenance as needed. I\u2019m hearing some noise coming from Dock Plate #3, but nothing serious at this point. I believe this can wait until the current projects are completed, but if not, I will contact an outside vendor to come in.\n\nBest,\nAgkop Baltagian",
    "status": "Closed and Completed",
    "material_cost": "0",
    "labor_time": "1.5",
    "work_performed_by": "Dennis Davis",
    "assigned_to": "Maintenance",
    "downtime_hours": "0",
    "completed_datetime": "12/17/2025 09:45 AM",
    "comments": "Dennis Davis - 12/17/25  9:23:36 AM: The noise appeared to be from cavitation due to the lack of hydraulic fluids and that stemmed from a loose fitting on a hydraulic piston.\nFilled with oil and lubricated all hinge areas. It is working fine | Dennis Davis - 12/15/25  7:59:52 AM: Bay #3 is scheduled to be empty Wednesday 12/17/2025 so I can look under and see what is wrong",
    "attachments": []
  },
  {
    "equipment_id": "1808",
    "equipment_eq_id": "EQ ID 1808",
    "equipment_name": "Bay #4",
    "department": "Shipping",
    "wo_id": "15136",
    "date_notified": "03/21/2025",
    "urgency": "5. Prod Ongoing, Maint Required",
    "problem": "Good afternoon Maintenance team,\n\nThe dock plate for Dock Door #4 is not fully bending down when we try to close it. We\u2019re okay for now since we have a swap scheduled for Monday, but could you please take a look at it first thing Monday morning?\n\nWhen pressing the button to raise the plate and then slowly lowering it, the plate doesn\u2019t align properly and doesn\u2019t settle at the correct angle hence not properly closing.\n\nBest,\nAgkop Baltagian",
    "status": "Closed and Completed",
    "material_cost": "0",
    "labor_time": "0.5",
    "work_performed_by": "Preston/Dennis",
    "assigned_to": "Maintenance",
    "downtime_hours": "0",
    "completed_datetime": "03/24/2025 02:00 PM",
    "comments": "Preston Ellexson - 03/25/25  4:11:19 AM: Had Agkop get the trailer moved. Went down, lifted bay, and set maintenance latch. Checked oil level, and for any leaks. Level in reservoir is good and there aren't any leaks. Sprayed cylinder with chain/cable lube. After looking further, the hinge pin the mounts the kick plate to the cylinder had shifted. One of the cotter pins that hold the hinge pin in was missing. We used a pry bar to get the pin resituated and put a new cotter pin on the missing side. Tested and everything is working the way it should now. Dock is ok to use. | Dennis Davis - 03/24/25  4:21:52 AM: We went to check the dock plate first thing this morning 03/21/2025 but there is a truck parked in #4 and we can't do anything until it is moved.",
    "attachments": []
  },
