  {
    "equipment_id": "1813",
    "equipment_eq_id": "EQ ID 1813",
    "equipment_name": "Shipping Office",
    "department": "Shipping",
    "wo_id": "20061",
    "date_notified": "07/09/2026",
    "urgency": "2. General Maint - High Priority",
    "problem": "AC is not working in the shipping office.",
    "status": "Closed and Completed",
    "material_cost": "1100",
    "labor_time": "6",
    "work_performed_by": "Preston/Johnson's Heating & Air",
    "assigned_to": "Maintenance",
    "downtime_hours": "0",
    "completed_datetime": "07/23/2026 02:30 PM",
    "comments": "Preston Ellexson - 08/17/26  5:04:42 AM: Had Johnson's Heating & Air come out. Caleb said it wasn't hitting the high side pressure it needed. Since the fan wouldn't kick on high, he couldn't determine if the freon level was good or not. Agkop was gone, so I got with Karen and Randy on replacing it with a new one. I found a good one on Amazon. Went ahead and stepped up to a 1.5-ton unit instead of the one-ton unit. Got Pam to order so it could be here next week. Removed the old one and trashed. New one arrived Tuesday. Had to shift this install around for 2 days due to fab machinery issues. Got all installed. Lines have been ran out the building and everything is ready to turn on. Got with Johnson's and they are coming out tmrw morning. We found a slight leak when turning on to test. Caleb said this is pretty normal on these systems. Got leak fixed and had them pull the vacuum on it for 20-30 minutes. Mini split is working well with no issues. We had a very slight dripping start the next day. I removed the cover. It was just the lines condensating a bit. I fit the insulation over them better and taped all the way around. No more dripping. Unit is running great.",
    "attachments": []
  },
