    "comments": "Preston Ellexson - 04/17/25  5:43:17 AM: We decided with the 480V power in question to not add in the new charger. Got the old charger removed from service. Removed the barrier, plugged the electrical box opening, and cleaned area. | Preston Ellexson - 08/27/24  4:14:56 AM: The stand-up chargers are ran on 240V. Most new chargers run on 480V only. I will have to see if we have a circuit I can add this on. I don't really want to add it to the existing 2 chargers. They pull around 23A max capacity, so I'm worried the wires/conduit are too small to add this to. | Preston Ellexson - 08/05/24 10:07:42 AM: This is a low priority right now as we have plenty of chargers per lifts when needed. The new forklift replaced one of our stand-up lifts so eventually we will only have one stand-up lift to my understanding. I will get this new charger swapped out with one of the old stand-up lift chargers this week hopefully.",
