    "downtime_hours": "0",
    "completed_datetime": "06/12/2024 01:30 PM",
    "comments": "Preston Ellexson - 06/12/24 12:05:36 PM: Locked machine out. Removed cover on bottom for belt tensioner. Released tension. Removed motor/gearbox assembly. Got the gearbox replaced. Swapped mounting brackets to the new gearbox. Put pulley and sleeve back on. Got tightened at the right shaft depth. Topped off with 460 gear oil. Remounted the motor/gearbox. Got belt put on pulley. Tightened gearbox mounts and adjusted the tension of the turntable belt. Got everything tight and all covers back on. Tested with no issues. Machine is very quite compared to before. For the stopping issue, I found a shoulder bolt at bottom of the film assembly that was almost fully unthreaded. Got it tightened back up. Tightened 2 more bolts on the outside roller assembly that affect the end wrap. When the roller shifts out to move the film towards the auto-cutter, it had slop with those bolts being loose. Tested 5 or 6 pallets and they wrapped from start to finish with no issues. | Preston Ellexson - 02/22/24 10:30:19 AM: Tech has been here since 10:30 inspecting and doing PM's on the machine. | Preston Ellexson - 02/21/24  4:06:41 AM: Tech will be here tomorrow or Friday to inspect machine. | Preston Ellexson - 02/16/24  6:37:55 AM: I am getting a tech scheduled to come look at this. It will be a few weeks more than likely, but it is in process.",
    "attachments": []
  },
  {
