    "comments": "Preston Ellexson - 08/05/24  7:19:59 AM: Removed side door. No voltage incoming. These are plugged into a GFCI by the beam. Tested and reset a couple times. Turned machine on. Main roller had wrapping all around it. This probably caused the machine to trip because it would've just kept wrapping up tighter and creating too much tension. Got this cleaned off and checked everything else on the machine. Had Lisa wrap a few pallets with no issues. Nobody had anymore needed wrapping at the time. Machine is running good right now.",
    "attachments": []
  },
