    "labor_time": "1.5",
    "work_performed_by": "Preston/James@Medley",
    "assigned_to": "Maintenance",
    "downtime_hours": "0",
    "completed_datetime": "02/18/2026 10:00 AM",
    "comments": "Preston Ellexson - 02/18/26  8:12:22 AM: James came out and we found it was just a faulty toggle switch. I told him not to worry about it and I would take care of it. I removed the steering wheel cover and the fuse. The switch was so tight, I could not get it loose with any pliers. I brought the panel to maintenance, broke the switch, and slowly ground off the jamb nut. Put a spacer washer on the inside of the cover and installed switch as needed. Put the fuse in and put the cover back on. Tested and the lights are working great. Everything is back on and ready for use. | Preston Ellexson - 02/16/26 12:14:13 PM: James will be back out this week to finish 2 other repairs. I'll have him look into this when he comes.",
    "attachments": []
  },
