    "completed_datetime": "09/23/2026 10:00 AM",
    "comments": "Preston Ellexson - 09/23/26  8:03:43 AM: Our new charger isn't usable here. I never looked at it when we got the new lift, because we didn't have the availability to add 480V in that location. Charger is for 48V batteries, and not 36V. I am reaching out to the vendor to see what our options are for returning/swapping. I am also reaching out to Wells Industrial Battery to have Arley come out and inspect the faulty charger. | Preston Ellexson - 09/23/26  8:03:00 AM: The charger isn't turning on. Power and fuses are good, but I haven't checked much further into this. I have to see if I can swap out the charger with a new one we have. If not, I'll have to call a tech to inspect the faulty one. I will follow-up on this tomorrow. | Preston Ellexson - 08/31/26 10:20:25 AM: Operator informed me the Raymond chargers were not on and working. The disconnect was off. Someone probably thought it was the one for the fans. I turned it back on. The Hawker charger on bottom is lighting up, but no screen. Hopefully it's something simple like a fuse, but I'll have to check it to see if I need to get with our Forklift Battery vendor. Top charger is working with no issues.",
    "attachments": []
  },
