    "downtime_hours": "0",
    "completed_datetime": "11/19/2024 09:00 AM",
    "comments": "Preston Ellexson - 11/25/24  7:11:56 AM: James came out and inspected. One of the contactors wasn't de-energizing the way it should. It was reading that the foot brake was engaged at all times so it wouldn't let the throttle respond. He got it swapped out and tested. Lift is running good. Returned to shipping.",
    "attachments": []
  },
  {
    "equipment_id": "1590",
    "equipment_eq_id": "EQ ID 1590",
    "equipment_name": "Electric Forklift #1 (Clark)",
    "department": "Shipping",
    "wo_id": "15398",
    "date_notified": "04/16/2025",
    "urgency": "6. General Maint",
    "problem": "Hello Maintenance team,\n\nCan we please inspect the shipping forklifts and determine if we should start paperwork for a new forklift that we had budgeted for this year? Feel free not to include newer forklifts like the Toyota.\n\nSome questions to ask: \n1) Do we foresee that the forklifts will be operational for this fiscal year (up to november)\n2) Is there a forklift that we have been spending way too much to maintain?\n3) Are there any lingering safety issues ex. emergency breake being loose, etc.",
    "status": "Closed and Completed",
    "material_cost": "0",
    "labor_time": "1",
    "work_performed_by": "Preston",
    "assigned_to": "Maintenance",
    "downtime_hours": "0",
    "completed_datetime": "04/22/2025 07:30 AM",
    "comments": "Preston Ellexson - 04/22/25  5:32:33 AM: 1.) Our lifts should all be operational for the remainder of the fiscal year. The stand-up is the oldest lift in service, and the only repairs we schedule are all for normal wear items. Aside from an unforeseen break downs, all forklifts look good.\n2.) We have spent a significant amount of money on repairs for the shipping Clark sit down lift. Starting in late 2023 we began having brake issues. We had numerous on site repairs. We sent the lift to Medley in OKC at least 3 times in a 6-9 month period due to onsite work not being an option to repair. There were complete brake replacements twice. Both drive motors had repairs done. We've spent 10-15K or more at minimum since late 2023. The mirrors forklift was bought at the same time, and has not had any of these repairs done or needed to this day just for comparison.\n3.) I don't see any lingering safety issues right now. After the above was fully repaired, it has just been normal wear items on all lifts that have needed repaired. \nLet me know if there are any more questions or concerns on the forklifts.",
    "attachments": []
  },
  {
    "equipment_id": "1590",
    "equipment_eq_id": "EQ ID 1590",
    "equipment_name": "Electric Forklift #1 (Clark)",
    "department": "Shipping",
    "wo_id": "15415",
    "date_notified": "04/17/2025",
    "urgency": "5. Prod Ongoing, Maint Required",
    "problem": "The backup light is beeping continuously.",
    "status": "Closed and Completed",
    "material_cost": "0",
