    "assigned_to": "Maintenance",
    "downtime_hours": "0",
    "completed_datetime": "07/15/2026 09:30 AM",
    "comments": "Preston Ellexson - 07/30/26  8:09:05 AM: Ground off the welds to both handles. These are also here to keep the seat in a stationary upright position. With them gone, you can lean back further. The operators didn't have an issue with this. Got all welds ground down. Deburred everything needed where an operator could get cut. Took the lift back to shipping and all is working good. | Preston Ellexson - 07/09/26  7:40:25 AM: I got with Karen and Agkop on this. I'll get it done after my lunch while Charles is on his lunch.",
    "attachments": []
  },
  {
    "equipment_id": "1590",
    "equipment_eq_id": "EQ ID 1590",
    "equipment_name": "Electric Forklift #1 (Clark)",
    "department": "Shipping",
    "wo_id": "19910",
    "date_notified": "06/19/2026",
    "urgency": "6. General Maint",
    "problem": "Hello Maintenance team,\n\nCan you please take a look at the Clark. Headlights are not coming on and it seems like there is a shorting of sorts. Not a barrier to utilize in the building but good to have when going into a trailer which is typically darker especially during a thunderstorm day.\n\nBest,\nAgkop Baltagian",
    "status": "Closed and Completed",
    "material_cost": "0",
    "labor_time": "2",
    "work_performed_by": "James@Medley",
    "assigned_to": "Maintenance",
    "downtime_hours": "0",
    "completed_datetime": "07/31/2026 10:00 AM",
    "comments": "Preston Ellexson - 08/12/26  5:46:08 AM: James came back out a week later and realized that Medley sent him the wrong converter. He got the right one ordered, and sent the other back for refund. He came out the next week and swapped the converter out. This didn't fix the lights still. He went ahead and returned it as well and put the old converter back on. He ordered a switch while looking through the wiring schematic over the next weekend. Came out and swapped the switch when he got it. Lights are working good now with no issues. Sent lift back to shipping. | Preston Ellexson - 07/06/26  5:16:42 AM: James came out to inspect the lift. He determined it was the converter on this. He said there is little to no voltage coming out of it. He ordered one last week. He should be out this week to swap and test the lift. | Dennis Davis - 06/19/26 11:55:46 AM: This lift is showing the same symptoms as one that was in mirrors and after looking the other one up, Preston and I have decided\nthat it is most likely the dc converter, and we are going to call the forklift tech to look at it for us because we do not have parts in house.",
    "attachments": []
  },
